marks.l4:11:1-41:
  The @ends-because above `monthly rent` says why it comes to an end:
  
    Alex stops renting one day
  
  `monthly rent` can start itself again, but I could check that it comes to an end: each new copy waits, for an event or for time to pass, so a run over a list of events reaches an answer.
  So the mark changes nothing.
