  `instalments` can start itself again, but I could check that it comes to an end: each time round, one of its inputs gets smaller, towards a stop.
  So the mark changes nothing.
marks.l4:32:1-58:
  The @ends-because above `days left` says why it comes to an end:
  
    each step moves one day nearer the end date
  
  `days left` uses itself again, directly or through other rules, but not through a HENCE or LEST, and L4 gives no warning about whether a rule like that comes to an end.
  So the mark changes nothing. That reason is what a reader should check.
